  ],
  "difficulty": 1,
  "marks": 1,
  "estimatedSeconds": 90,
  "stem": "It is known that $y = Ax^n$, where $A$ and $n$ are constants. Which graph is a straight line?",
  "options": [
   {
    "key": "A",
    "content": "$\\lg y$ against $\\lg x$",
    "correct": true,
    "rationale": "Correct: $\\lg y = n\\lg x + \\lg A$ has the form $Y = mX + c$."
   },
   {
    "key": "B",
    "content": "$y$ against $\\lg x$",
    "rationale": "Only the right-hand side has been transformed; $y = A x^n$ is not linear in $\\lg x$."
   },
   {
    "key": "C",
    "content": "$\\lg y$ against $x$",
    "rationale": "That straightens $y = Ab^x$, where the unknown is in the index."
   },
   {
    "key": "D",
    "content": "$y$ against $x$",
    "rationale": "$y = Ax^n$ is a curve unless $n = 1$."
   }
  ],
  "explanation": "Take logarithms: $\\lg y = \\lg A + n\\lg x$. With $Y = \\lg y$ and $X = \\lg x$ this is $Y = nX + \\lg A$, a straight line with gradient $n$.",
